{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Then</b> [אדין]: a polel form, like מנצח." "<b>You have done</b> [עשית]: he counts it like עָשִׁתְנוּתָיו. Thus עָשִׂיתִי עָשָׂרָה, as I explained in <i>Sefer HaMispar</i>."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra parses the Aramaic word אדין ('then') as related to the Hebrew root נצח in the polel; the logic of the comparison is characteristically compressed.", 1 "The form עשתנותיו and the phrase עשיתי עשרה are quoted in Hebrew script as Ibn Ezra cites them; the grammatical point concerns conjugational patterns and is left untranslated where the Hebrew form itself is the subject of discussion."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:07.173223372Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}